<h2>About Beyond SR 513</h2>

<p>
  Beyond SR 513 is a volunteer-led advocacy effort started by residents of
  northeast Seattle who walk, bike, and take the bus along Sand Point Way NE.
</p>

<p>
  SR 513 was the state highway designation for this road until it was
  transferred to the city.  The name of our group is a reminder that the
  community &mdash; and the road itself &mdash; can move <em>beyond</em> its
  highway-era design.
</p>

<p>
  We work with the Seattle Department of Transportation, the Seattle City
  Council, and community organisations to advocate for safe, walkable, and
  bikeable streets along this corridor.
</p>
